<title>QATAR: Qatar Insurance net dips, announces bonus issue.</title>
<headline>Qatar Insurance net dips, announces bonus issue.</headline>
<dateline>DOHA 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(million riyals unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit		   51.53   vs     54.74</p>
<p>Total income		 74.51   vs     78.63</p>
<p>Expenses		     22.98   vs     23.89</p>
<p>Total cash dividend	22.5    vs     40.5</p>
<p>Bonus share issue	   9.0    vs     none</p>
<p>Shareholders' Equity    401.57   vs    373.62</p>
<p>Total Assets		562.97   vs    556.7</p>
<p>Full Name:  Qatar Insurance Company</p>
<p>Note: Shareholders agreed to distribute cash dividends equal to 25 percent of the paid-up capital and issue one bonus share for every nine held on December 31, 1996. QIC is 12 percent owned by the state and 88 percent by Qatari citizens and institutions.</p>
</text>
